  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In aniline&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a strong activating group. So, on direct bromination, substitution will occur at all ortho and para positions. And also we can not use lewis acid since it will react with lewis acid. But if we first convert this into amide then only para substitution will be major product.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cac2fee0-4bb6-437d-b296-0e7a3b66c868-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 300px;\" /></p>",
